{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/13006-demons-and-other-supernaturals","id":13006,"title":"Demons and other supernaturals","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-17T15:41:32-08:00","id":13006,"title":"Demons and other supernaturals","content":"So what do you think the demons will react to other supernaturals","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T16:11:25-08:00","id":13027,"title":"","content":"There is an entire section on this in the full text.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T17:24:33-08:00","id":13070,"title":"","content":"Oh my, yes. I particularly like the Nonspecific Guardian's opinion of the Arisen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;Seven deadly sins/Seven ways to win/Seven holy paths to hell/And your trip begins/Seven downward slopes/Seven bloodied hopes/Seven are your burning fires/Seven your desires&quot; \u2014 Iron Maiden,</i> Moonchild","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1122-the-grim-lich","name":"The Grim Lich","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T18:55:31-08:00","id":13114,"title":"","content":"I do kind of wish that they had all the factions comment about all the types of supernaturals, but I guess it is really just fluff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T23:15:20-08:00","id":13208,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it'd be cool to see how every group thought about all the other supers, but... well, that'd add word count, and they've already got an absolutely massive preview PDF. Although I'm beginning to wonder if a Sword's response to the Arisen wouldn't be something along the lines of &quot;I killed you. I killed you, like, twenty times. WHY WON'T YOU DIE?!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;Seven deadly sins/Seven ways to win/Seven holy paths to hell/And your trip begins/Seven downward slopes/Seven bloodied hopes/Seven are your burning fires/Seven your desires&quot; \u2014 Iron Maiden,</i> Moonchild","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1122-the-grim-lich","name":"The Grim Lich","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T08:26:35-08:00","id":13404,"title":"","content":"The problem with group stereotypes is most of the time they really aren't very useful for game given the word count dedicated to them. Either the group really doesn't have much to say about another given group, or the thought is kind of obvious. It'd be one thing if there was some kind of surprising twist in a given relationship, but mostly it's the same old &quot;Werewolves are really tough*&quot; and &quot;Vampires sure are clueless idiots**&quot;, with a solid &quot;...a what?&quot; for anything more exotic. Mostly noise; not really information.<br /> <br /> *Which gets silly with how untrue this claim has been for some time.<br /> **This is something I'd like to see go away. I don't necessarily want to see more vampire crossover but vampires being the clueless boobs of the occult world really wears on their cool factor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T09:32:08-08:00","id":13440,"title":"","content":"In general I agree with Wolfgar on this point. <br /> <br /> Stereotypes are just that, wide sweeping generalizations that let us partition of information in a manageable way and are pre-loaded with (usually) incorrect ideas. Plus it seems that every splat seems to have the same sorta stereotypes about each other splat -<br /> <br /> Vampires are self-absorbed and have no idea what is really going on. <br /> Werewolves are tough and primal.<br /> Mages have a lot of power but don't use it properly or they don't see as much of the &quot;big picture&quot; as they think<br /> Etc..<br /> <br /> I've run a lot of crossover campaigns. Including a Hunter campaign that involved every splat published at that point (so it lacked Mummy's and Unchained), including all the minor templates and one of monsters. It was an utter mess, fun as all hell, but a very messy feeling world even with all the effort I put in to it for consistent sake and to have sense of verisimilitude. <br /> <br /> Ever since I've been of the opinion that crossing over more then 2 game lines in any one campaign generally leads to the themes of each game getting damaged. Likewise, I think it can lead to the dreaded &quot;super-friends&quot; situation pretty easily without a strong guiding hand from the ST. For one-offs and sort couple of sessions things I'm still happy to throw the whole of the NWoD in a blender, but for long-term campaigns I really think two game lines crossing over is the max. <br /> <br /> Its still a bit of a tight-rope act to get it right. I am running a Mummy/Changeling game at current. I really screwed up the focus about a third of the way though the &quot;first act&quot; and it came of as Mummy with Changeling elements. I had to readdress the thematic balance quite a bit. Yet I still think that both games interacting with one another really heightened the theme they both share: Identity. <br /> <br /> When I run Demon its going to be a &quot;pure&quot; demon game I think. With no other major splats involved. Yet if I was going to crossover with another game line it would be one of the following -<br /> <br /> Mage<br /> Promethean<br /> Changeling<br /> <br /> I don't think the other 5 game lines really play well with Demon. Werewolf and Geist are too focused on one aspect of the WoD, plus Werewolf is very caught up in its own law that does not necessarily gel well with the new Demon fluff. Mummy might as well be its own isolated setting as its own fluff and metaplot (an arguable term) make it very hard to cross over with anything. Vampire rarely benefits from crossing over with any of the other games (with the possible exception of Hunter and Mummy) and Demon is no exception. At best the espionage and paranoia of Demon just adds to the political and tense feeling of Vampire, but no to an extent I feel Vampire could not achieve on its own. <br /> <br /> Hunter is the odd one out here really. You could cross it over, but then you would have to think about what parts of Hunter really add to Demon and cherry pick those. Trying to throw the whole of Hunter into Demon will not work I feel. <br /> <br /> All the above is obviously just my opinion, but its drawn from some experience with this stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T14:07:48-08:00","id":14278,"title":"","content":"Sorry what i meant was how the supernatural would react to the angels","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T18:59:26-08:00","id":14448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reaperfrost8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/13006-demons-and-other-supernaturals?p=14278#post14278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry what i meant was how the supernatural would react to the angels</div> </div> </div> </div>Right... that's really not the same question you asked at the start of this thread but here's a stab at it anyway. <br /> <br /> I think the point is that most supernatural creatures simply don't notice Angels. They are given pretty much perfect (if flimsy) Cover by the Infrastructure that summoned them. They appear perfectly normal in most respects. Other times they are not even physically present, instead possessing Humans to carry out their work. <br /> <br /> So to summarize a bit more and engage with the idea that other Supernaturals might at some point discover/run into an Angel -<br /> <br /> Vampires - Most probably chalk it up to &quot;weird shit&quot; in the world. Depending on the Angel's appearance the Lancea Et Sanctum might revere or fear it in particular. Likewise, a similar response may result from interaction with the Circle of the Crone (though as an aspect or embodiment/visitation of their chosen deity). Dragons might actually try to study it and I imagine sometimes that Infrastructure and Wyrms Nests might cross-over. <br /> <br /> Werewolves - Likely to think its a spirit of some kind. Particularly if they catch it possessing someone. Likely surprised when it does not seem native to the Shadow either once (if) they force it back to the other side of the Gauntlet. <br /> <br /> Mages - Similar to Vampires in that it likely starts off in the &quot;weird shit&quot; category for most of them. Prime I believe gives the ability to interact with God Machine stuff (which has some worrying metaphysical implications I might add) so an Obrimos Mysterium member is likely to find the whole thing interesting so long as its not trying to kill him. <br /> <br /> Promethean - Mistake it for a Quashilim, this has happened at least once in cannon. <br /> <br /> Changeling - Likely mistake it for a True Fae (enough of them have Angel motifs) or ones weird pet/servant. <br /> <br /> Hunter - Really, really depends on the cell in question. Tier one groups that are religious may think its on their side depending on the context and how it looks. Tier two and three groups will each react differently. The Mallues Malificum and the Long Night might support the Angel. Cheiron will want to strip it for parts. The Lucifuge will run away screaming or cower in a corner (they are terrified of angels in the fluff). <br /> <br /> Geist - I'm not sure. Never played Geist and only read the 1.0 core before revisions so I've never got a great feel for the game. Pretty sure you could not mistake an Angel for a Ghost or Underworld entity. <br /> <br /> Mummy - Does the Angel prevent the Mummy from following his primary purpose? If the answer is no then the Mummy is likely to ignore or wearily analyze the Angel as best it can. If so the Mummy will stomp the Angel if it can and move on. <br /> <br /> Obviously, once again these are just my own opinions on the matter. I'm sure other people have more well thought out examples and explanations then I.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-19T22:07:35-08:00","id":14535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/13006-demons-and-other-supernaturals?p=13114#post13114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do kind of wish that they had all the factions comment about all the types of supernaturals, but I guess it is really just fluff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, the one comment about meeting a changeling &quot;who's warm to the touch and smells like a summer bonfire&quot; made me think of something... Aside from the Aura Sight form ability, do demons even <i>have</i> the sort of sensory powers which would pierce the Mask?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">(Previously known by the name of &quot;GrimGent&quot;.)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/335-the-yann-waters","name":"The Yann Waters","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T18:39:55-08:00","id":15035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Yann Waters</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/13006-demons-and-other-supernaturals?p=14535#post14535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, the one comment about meeting a changeling &quot;who's warm to the touch and smells like a summer bonfire&quot; made me think of something... Aside from the Aura Sight form ability, do demons even <i>have</i> the sort of sensory powers which would pierce the Mask?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to my knowledge, but I've only skimmed their powers section. From what I can tell Demons are about as good at hiding as Changelings. However compared with Mages and Mummy's they don't have that much stuff that spots supernatural stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"color:#0000cd\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><i>&quot;There is no God in the Badlands.&quot; </i></span></span></span><span style=\"font-family:helvetica, arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">- Sunny</span></span><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img41/8167/obcp.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/599-hawthorn","name":"Hawthorn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar599_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"511"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T20:07:35-08:00","id":15074,"title":"","content":"A handful of vampires likely accidentally worships/works for the God-Machine. Vampirism is lousy with cults and and similar groups; at least a few of those probably serve the God-Machine indirectly.<br /> <br /> Werewolves will assume a hostile spirit. (Updates to Werewolf may make them angel savvy as I believe angels are core book, not just demon, so the Forsaken may gain some anti-Angel abilities.)<br /> <br /> Mages are too varied to say, but I would assume mages worshiping them, serving them in exchange for knowledge, hunting them, and trying to bond them with theurgical magic would all be common reactions.<br /> <br /> Prometheans will likely just be confused.<br /> <br /> Changelings assume True Fae and panic.<br /> <br /> Hunters are too varied to tell. Hunt, kill, capture, study, serve, worship, molest...<br /> <br /> Mummies and angels both share a singularity of purpose so the primary question becomes how compatible those purposes are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1136-wolfgar","name":"Wolfgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"646"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T10:34:25-08:00","id":15467,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolfgar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/13006-demons-and-other-supernaturals?p=15074#post15074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A handful of vampires likely accidentally worships/works for the God-Machine. Vampirism is lousy with cults and and similar groups; at least a few of those probably serve the God-Machine indirectly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or directly: let's not forget the Holy Engineers from <i>Danse Macabre</i>. Their covenant's beliefs tie heavily into the Marco Singe version of what's going on, complete with prayer-signals directed to the constellation of Orion, vampires being burned by &quot;the solar broadcast&quot; because the Fury at the center of the sun hates them, and plans to recover the &quot;Packet Theta&quot; retrieved from the moon by the US space program.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">(Previously known by the name of &quot;GrimGent&quot;.)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/335-the-yann-waters","name":"The Yann Waters","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-01T07:44:49-08:00","id":21153,"title":"","content":"There are some suggestions in dealing with the other Supernaturals on pages 75-77 of the Kickstarter preview under &quot;Outside Agents&quot;. It doesn't cover Geist or Mummy right now, but there is nothing stopping a GM from writing them in for their own stories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1428-sicol","name":"Sicol","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}